WEBVTT

00:04.660 --> 00:08.770
<b>Oh God, forgive me...</b>

00:09.270 --> 00:12.480
<b>Forgive me for staining the earth 
with the blood of my foes,</b>

00:12.480 --> 00:15.470
<b>and guide me to the promised land.</b>

00:16.270 --> 00:19.420
<b>I am but a poor, ignorant lamb.</b>

00:19.420 --> 00:21.960
<b>A lost lamb who is ignorant of the truth.</b>

00:23.600 --> 00:27.290
<b>I sing a song of praise unto the Lord.</b>

00:28.020 --> 00:35.060
<b>Oh, I praise the Lord. 
I praise the heart of the Lord.</b>

00:44.130 --> 00:48.270
<b>Fuck you. I'd prefer to 
feed you to the pigs.</b>

01:00.320 --> 01:02.280
<b>Attention, everyone!</b>

01:11.770 --> 01:14.830
<b>What a naughty girl you are.</b>

01:14.830 --> 01:18.550
<b>I'm so overcome with feeling, 
I can't control myself!</b>

01:26.920 --> 01:29.890
<b>My little fairy...</b>

01:44.930 --> 01:47.800
<b>You certainly made a mess of things.</b>

01:48.480 --> 01:51.350
<b>I regret acting out of line.</b>

01:54.650 --> 01:57.660
<b>But this is the will of God.</b>

01:57.660 --> 02:00.220
<b>She must be defeated...</b>

02:01.740 --> 02:04.410
<b>That demon!</b>

02:13.170 --> 02:14.860
<b>Are you serious?</b>

02:14.860 --> 02:17.730
<b>You're putting Lt. Colonel Degurechaff 
in charge of that combat team?</b>

02:19.030 --> 02:20.320
<b>Of course.</b>

02:20.320 --> 02:23.120
<b>In light of the current war situation,</b>

02:23.120 --> 02:25.490
<b>we've no choice but to put her
 in charge of her brainchild.</b>

02:25.490 --> 02:30.290
<b>But... behind that appearance
of a little girl...</b>

02:33.180 --> 02:34.760
<b>...is a monster.</b>

02:39.130 --> 02:41.230
<b>That's what you want to say, right?</b>

02:46.960 --> 02:50.070
<b>Welcome to my combat team!</b>

02:50.620 --> 02:54.070
<b>My wonderful comrades-in-arms, with whom 
I've enjoyed my time so much...</b>

02:54.300 --> 02:58.400
<b>Let us rejoice in our new comrades!</b>

02:58.860 --> 03:03.450
<b>And to those of you who are new, 
I welcome you with open arms.</b>

03:03.680 --> 03:08.150
<b>Welcome to my... to our battlefield.</b>

03:08.620 --> 03:10.870
<b>This world is unfair!</b>

03:10.870 --> 03:13.870
<b>And the battlefield is one 
insane thing after another!</b>

03:15.030 --> 03:17.430
<b>And for all of you, that means...</b>

03:17.430 --> 03:21.800
<b>You are now free... to choose!</b>

03:21.800 --> 03:24.910
<b>Choose whether to struggle or die!</b>

03:26.450 --> 03:28.950
<b>Welcome to the front lines!</b>

03:29.370 --> 03:31.980
<b>It's time for war!</b>

03:35.060 --> 03:39.990
<b>This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.</b>

03:36.200 --> 03:37.960
<b>How?</b>

03:37.960 --> 03:39.980
<b>How did this happen?</b>

03:39.990 --> 03:42.200
<b>Unified Year 1926, Autumn</b>

03:42.280 --> 03:48.370
<b>Eastern Front, Near the Front Lines</b>

03:50.240 --> 03:52.110
<b>We're in enemy firing range here, too!</b>

03:50.250 --> 03:57.710
<b>Imperial Army Salamander Combat Team Infantry Commander
Captain Lienhart Thon</b>

03:50.250 --> 03:57.710
<b>Imperial Army Salamander Combat Team Infantry XO
Lieutenant Klaus Tospan</b>

03:52.110 --> 03:53.550
<b>Give the order to retreat!</b>

03:53.550 --> 03:57.850
<b>No! The principle of elastic defense
requires us to defend this point!</b>

04:01.320 --> 04:04.400
<b>Our infantry are a bunch of dumbasses.</b>

04:04.400 --> 04:07.590
<b>What's the point of 
holing up in a trench <i>there</i>?</b>

04:13.260 --> 04:15.880
<b>Our allies are cut off! 
We need to protect them!</b>

04:13.270 --> 04:17.110
<b>Imperial Army Salamander Combat Team Armored Unit Commander
Captain Elmer Ahrens</b>

04:15.880 --> 04:17.800
<b>Annihilate the enemy forces!</b>

04:20.610 --> 04:23.490
<b><i>We're under attack! Fall back! Fall back!</i></b>

04:22.510 --> 04:25.630
<b>And our tanks are poorly trained dogs 
who don't even know how to sit?</b>

04:25.630 --> 04:29.400
<b>Our job right now isn't to attack! 
It's to recover our allies!</b>

04:29.400 --> 04:32.960
<b>Our allies' base has been surrounded! 
We will provide support!</b>

04:29.410 --> 04:34.290
<b>Imperial Army Salamander Combat Team Artillery Commander
Captain Rolf Meybert</b>

04:32.960 --> 04:34.890
<b>Artillery, full attack!</b>

04:39.660 --> 04:41.310
<b><i>We're out of shells!</i></b>

04:41.310 --> 04:42.060
<b><i>What?</i></b>

04:42.060 --> 04:44.810
<b>And my artillery is just 
a random group of morons!</b>

04:44.810 --> 04:49.180
<b>Have you even considered whether
that base is worth all those shells?</b>

04:49.180 --> 04:54.020
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 4th Company Commander
Lieutenant Theobald Wüstemann</b>

04:49.580 --> 04:51.700
<b>Hurry! Climb!</b>

04:51.700 --> 04:53.300
<b>Stay in formation!</b>

04:55.120 --> 04:59.280
<b>And our new mages aren't even 
worth using as human shields.</b>

05:01.130 --> 05:03.770
<b>They all work hard, but they're so dumb!</b>

05:03.770 --> 05:06.780
<b>Why am I in charge of this combat team?!</b>

05:06.780 --> 05:10.780
<b>Episode One:
Salamander Combat Team</b>

05:07.800 --> 05:09.940
<b>Fuck this!</b>

05:10.780 --> 05:19.210
<b>Imperial Army Strategic Headquarters 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion Commander and Salamander Combat Team Commander
Lt. Colonel Tanya von Degurechaff</b>

05:11.070 --> 05:14.540
<b>This is what happens when I had 
barely any time to train them.</b>

05:14.540 --> 05:16.800
<b>What a waste of time.</b>

05:16.800 --> 05:18.760
<b><i>Lieutenant Colonel! Fighters!</i></b>

05:19.200 --> 05:21.470
<b>Four of them, heading our way!</b>

05:22.000 --> 05:25.040
<b>Altitude 9500, speed 350!</b>

05:22.050 --> 05:25.050
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion XO
Lieutenant Viktoriya Ivanovna Serebryakov</b>

05:25.040 --> 05:27.270
<b>They're after our surface base!</b>

05:25.050 --> 05:30.010
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 3rd Company Commander
Captain Rhiner Neumann</b>

05:26.930 --> 05:30.010
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 2nd Company Commander
Captain Wilibald Koenig</b>

05:27.270 --> 05:30.000
<b>Lieutenant Grantz's unit is the closest! 
They're en route to provide support!</b>

05:30.000 --> 05:34.020
<b>We're moving as fast as we can, 
but those fighters will get there first!</b>

05:30.140 --> 05:32.470
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion 1st Company Commander
Lieutenant Warren Grantz</b>

05:42.240 --> 05:43.390
<b>Enemy fighters approaching!</b>

05:47.480 --> 05:49.360
<b>We can't hold this position!</b>

05:50.620 --> 05:53.710
<b>What the hell are those mages doing?</b>

06:06.020 --> 06:10.610
<b>Damn it. I told you not to slow me down.</b>

06:12.540 --> 06:13.990
<b>You got here fast.</b>

06:13.990 --> 06:16.750
<b>Sorry! We'll head to intercept.</b>

06:15.930 --> 06:16.920
<b>Wait.</b>

06:17.260 --> 06:20.470
<b>I'll do it. Let me give everyone 
a tactical demonstration.</b>

06:20.470 --> 06:21.950
<b>You'll do it personally?</b>

06:22.370 --> 06:25.690
<b>The Federation doesn't give 
its fighters a mage escort.</b>

06:25.690 --> 06:28.360
<b>The rest of you support 
the ground forces' retreat.</b>

06:37.450 --> 06:39.940
<b>Dog of the Empire! 
There's just one of you?</b>

06:39.940 --> 06:40.830
<b>You think you can take us?!</b>

06:51.280 --> 06:53.370
<b>That's the Commies I know!</b>

06:53.370 --> 06:56.390
<b>They love wasting bullets 
and soldiers' lives!</b>

06:58.300 --> 07:00.340
<b>How can she move like that?</b>

07:00.340 --> 07:01.890
<b>A named mage?</b>

07:01.890 --> 07:03.520
<b>The Devil of the Rhine?!</b>

07:18.340 --> 07:20.920
<b>I doubt anybody's learning 
anything from this shit.</b>

07:21.370 --> 07:22.710
<b>Enemy sighted!</b>

07:22.710 --> 07:25.420
<b>Show them what you learned 
in your training!</b>

07:30.930 --> 07:33.520
<b>I'm fighting here!</b>

07:33.520 --> 07:35.700
<b>Don't you know how to 
work with your allies?!</b>

07:35.700 --> 07:36.210
<b>Now!</b>

07:37.480 --> 07:39.980
<b>Die, monster!</b>

07:58.900 --> 08:00.730
<b>She knocked it out of the sky?</b>

08:00.730 --> 08:02.790
<b>That's what it looks like when 
you have the Silver Wings...</b>

08:03.790 --> 08:07.120
<b>No... It's hopeless!</b>

08:16.000 --> 08:18.420
<b>Oh, God!</b>

08:19.320 --> 08:22.030
<b>Even the fucking Commies are 
begging for God's help?</b>

08:22.030 --> 08:25.550
<b>I'm sick of people who keep 
clinging to the absurd.</b>

08:26.480 --> 08:30.610
<b>Oh, Lord, grant us balance and order.</b>

08:30.610 --> 08:33.770
<b>Grant us peace, and the promised land.</b>

08:34.350 --> 08:37.100
<b>You are the guiding shepherd.</b>

08:37.100 --> 08:41.040
<b>Guide us upon the path of hardship 
and lead us to the summit of the hill.</b>

08:41.380 --> 08:44.170
<b>You are the promised crown of glory,</b>

08:44.170 --> 08:45.530
<b>the house of honor...</b>

08:45.530 --> 08:48.390
<b>A world of peace and purity.</b>

08:49.370 --> 08:53.420
<b>May your gospel resound upon the Earth...</b>

08:54.080 --> 08:56.590
<b>Upon the world.</b>

09:13.380 --> 09:16.610
<b>Shit. Why the hell do 
I have to praise God?</b>

09:17.030 --> 09:19.520
<b>That bastard's trying to brainwash me.</b>

09:20.380 --> 09:22.000
<b><i>This is 02.</i></b>

09:22.000 --> 09:24.480
<b><i>Our surface forces have 
completed their withdrawal.</i></b>

09:24.480 --> 09:25.760
<b>Roger that.</b>

09:26.520 --> 09:28.880
<b>Everyone, return to base immediately.</b>

09:29.250 --> 09:33.620
<b><i>Also, it seems our new recruits 
don't know how to fight a war yet.</i></b>

09:34.340 --> 09:38.490
<b><i>Once we're back, I want every 
single unit commander in my tent.</i></b>

09:38.970 --> 09:41.680
<b>Salamander Combat Team Garrison</b>

09:42.230 --> 09:46.100
<b>Captain Ahrens. Why did you 
send in your tanks?</b>

09:46.100 --> 09:49.410
<b>Does the concept of "reserve forces" 
mean nothing to you?</b>

09:50.140 --> 09:54.200
<b>And Captain Meybert, it seems you don't 
know how valuable an artillery shell is.</b>

09:54.200 --> 09:58.080
<b>If I start deducting from your salary,
will that get it through your head?</b>

09:58.720 --> 10:01.800
<b>And Captain Thon and Lieutenant Tospan, 
are you simply stupid?</b>

10:01.800 --> 10:04.000
<b>Why would you try to hole up 
in a forward position?</b>

10:04.000 --> 10:06.710
<b>On the Eastern Front, defending 
our camp is our highest priority.</b>

10:07.810 --> 10:11.350
<b>And Wüstemann, your maximum air time 
is still in the double digits?</b>

10:11.350 --> 10:12.710
<b>That's pathetic.</b>

10:12.710 --> 10:15.370
<b>You're gonna get shot down 
within the day at this rate.</b>

10:16.210 --> 10:17.860
<b>Let me make this as clear as I can.</b>

10:17.860 --> 10:21.200
<b>Our forces pride themselves on our speed.</b>

10:21.200 --> 10:23.800
<b>But this front is huge, and we...</b>

10:24.610 --> 10:26.220
<b>We can only defend a single point.</b>

10:26.220 --> 10:28.790
<b>Thus, we need to make that point strong.</b>

10:28.790 --> 10:33.990
<b>If we can't do that, our already depleted
 forces will be isolated and wiped out.</b>

10:33.990 --> 10:37.460
<b>B-But ma'am, if we stay in our camp 
we'll be surrounded!</b>

10:37.460 --> 10:41.780
<b>Elastic defense theory teaches us 
to never give up the initiative!</b>

10:41.780 --> 10:43.740
<b>Shut up, textbook for brains!</b>

10:44.120 --> 10:47.580
<b>The elastic defense theory you were taught</b>

10:47.580 --> 10:50.750
<b>only works under conditions 
of adequate manpower,</b>

10:50.750 --> 10:53.250
<b>adequate equipment, and adequate supply!</b>

10:53.560 --> 10:57.340
<b>And here on the Eastern Front, 
that's impossible.</b>

10:57.340 --> 11:02.260
<b>But you lot refuse to accept that reality.</b>

11:02.260 --> 11:03.820
<b>Sheesh.</b>

11:03.820 --> 11:08.060
<b>There's nothing worse than someone 
who's stubborn, stupid, and hardworking.</b>

11:10.430 --> 11:14.290
<b><i>The war began with the Entente Alliance 
violating our borders.</i></b>

11:14.290 --> 11:17.250
<b><i>Now it's spread to the whole continent.</i></b>

11:18.480 --> 11:21.570
<b><i>We occupied the northern 
Entente Alliance territories,</i></b>

11:21.570 --> 11:23.900
<b><i>but now the partisans 
are fighting back hard.</i></b>

11:24.410 --> 11:26.020
<b><i>And down on the southern continent,</i></b>

11:26.020 --> 11:30.040
<b><i>we're still fighting a group 
calling itself the Free Republic.</i></b>

11:32.860 --> 11:35.680
<b><i>Our war against the Federation 
on the eastern front</i></b>

11:35.680 --> 11:38.060
<b><i>shows every sign of 
turning into a quagmire.</i></b>

11:39.170 --> 11:44.650
<b>We are taking heavy losses at 
the hands of the Imperial Army.</b>

11:39.550 --> 11:46.970
<b>Somewhere in Moskva, People's Party Conference Room</b>

11:44.650 --> 11:50.980
<b>And those who allowed this to happen 
must suffer the people's wrath!</b>

11:50.980 --> 11:55.740
<b>And thus, we must come together!</b>

11:55.730 --> 11:57.480
<b>Party Leader
Comrade Secretary Josef</b>

11:57.470 --> 12:01.330
<b>We must give our former 
comrades a chance to atone!</b>

11:57.480 --> 12:06.490
<b>People's Commissariat for Internal Affairs Committee Member
Comrade Loria</b>

12:01.330 --> 12:04.270
<b>We must bring in the 
mages that we sent away</b>

12:04.270 --> 12:06.490
<b>for the crime of siding 
with the old order!</b>

12:08.040 --> 12:13.490
<b>B-But the very existence of mages 
goes against party principles.</b>

12:13.490 --> 12:17.790
<b>Oh? Comrade, are you saying 
that you're opposed to having</b>

12:17.790 --> 12:21.500
<b>these counterrevolutionary elements 
fight the Imperial Army?</b>

12:21.500 --> 12:24.410
<b>N-No! I just...</b>

12:26.000 --> 12:28.010
<b>Comrade Secretary,</b>

12:28.010 --> 12:31.930
<b>I am free to proceed with bringing 
the mages into the army, yes?</b>

12:32.730 --> 12:37.840
<b><i>And to the west, the Allied Kingdom 
maintains air superiority,</i></b>

12:37.840 --> 12:40.360
<b><i>while it attempts to find 
new methods of cooperation.</i></b>

12:40.360 --> 12:42.690
<b>Allied Kingdom Capital, Whitehall</b>

12:43.910 --> 12:45.950
<b>So Prime Minister Churbull,</b>

12:45.950 --> 12:49.450
<b>Allied Kingdom Navy
Major General Donald Habergram</b>

12:45.950 --> 12:49.450
<b>you want to work more closely
 with the Federation?</b>

12:49.450 --> 12:56.460
<b>Allied Kingdom
Prime Minister Churbull</b>

12:51.690 --> 12:53.890
<b>Major General Habergram,</b>

12:53.890 --> 12:56.450
<b>you're an intelligence officer, 
so I expect you to understand.</b>

12:56.450 --> 13:01.090
<b>If we have to make a deal 
with the devil, so be it.</b>

13:01.760 --> 13:06.490
<b><i>I see. So we're making 
one devil fight another.</i></b>

13:07.620 --> 13:13.210
<b><i>The Ildoa Kingdom, which allied with
the Empire, maintains neutrality.</i></b>

13:13.210 --> 13:16.110
<b><i>Meanwhile, the Unified States, 
on the other side of the ocean,</i></b>

13:16.110 --> 13:19.930
<b><i>is providing support to our enemies 
in the form of weapons and supplies.</i></b>

13:19.930 --> 13:23.500
<b><i>They even sent in a multinational 
volunteer force.</i></b>

13:25.440 --> 13:30.910
<b>Gravesite Somewhere in Federation Territory</b>

13:27.390 --> 13:31.400
<b>Why can't we send them 
back to their homelands?</b>

13:31.860 --> 13:36.070
<b>The rule is that war dead 
are buried where they died.</b>

13:36.610 --> 13:39.660
<b>We can't cause problems for other 
countries in the middle of a war.</b>

13:39.670 --> 13:43.300
<b>Unified States Volunteer 
 Lieutenant Mary Sue</b>

13:40.370 --> 13:41.740
<b>But...</b>

13:41.740 --> 13:43.300
<b>It is what it is.</b>

13:44.010 --> 13:47.000
<b>A hero rests in the land where they fell.</b>

13:48.700 --> 13:54.490
<b><i>The Empire's enormous military might has 
made it the enemy of the whole world.</i></b>

13:55.950 --> 13:58.970
<b><i>Damn it. Why did this happen?</i></b>

13:59.380 --> 14:04.770
<b><i>I'd rather be training a bunch of 
penguins than those new recruits!</i></b>

14:04.770 --> 14:08.740
<b><i>Actually, in my old world, didn't some 
country give a penguin an honorary rank?</i></b>

14:31.710 --> 14:34.210
<b><i>The snow is impossibly beautiful,</i></b>

14:34.210 --> 14:36.030
<b><i>and impossibly merciless.</i></b>

14:36.490 --> 14:40.290
<b><i>I don't even need to recall what happened 
in the world war in my last world.</i></b>

14:42.180 --> 14:45.780
<b><i>Winter saps a soldier's strength, 
wears at their mind,</i></b>

14:45.780 --> 14:47.810
<b><i>and freezes their legs.</i></b>

14:48.690 --> 14:53.780
<b><i>And when the snow melts, it'll become mud 
that we'll have to wade through.</i></b>

14:54.690 --> 14:57.960
<b><i>The Empire's greatest 
strength is its mobility.</i></b>

14:57.960 --> 14:59.920
<b><i>This is the worst battlefield 
possible for it.</i></b>

15:02.240 --> 15:05.030
<b>We can't win like this.</b>

15:06.090 --> 15:07.970
<b>Emergency report, Lieutenant Colonel!</b>

15:07.970 --> 15:09.970
<b>What is it? What happened?</b>

15:09.970 --> 15:12.850
<b>Major Weiss encountered 
the enemy while on patrol.</b>

15:12.850 --> 15:16.480
<b>Two Federation infantry brigades 
are approaching fast!</b>

15:16.720 --> 15:18.740
<b>Two infantry brigades?!</b>

15:18.740 --> 15:19.480
<b>Yes.</b>

15:19.480 --> 15:22.970
<b>Major Weiss had the frontline 
units fall back.</b>

15:23.370 --> 15:26.400
<b>Good. He has my authorization.</b>

15:28.570 --> 15:30.290
<b>This is bad...</b>

15:30.290 --> 15:32.590
<b>We're going to be swallowed 
up at this rate.</b>

15:41.090 --> 15:42.150
<b>Men!</b>

15:42.490 --> 15:44.340
<b>The situation is simple!</b>

15:44.340 --> 15:47.980
<b>A huge enemy army is 
about to surround us!</b>

15:48.570 --> 15:52.030
<b>We have no choice but to let them attack, 
wait for them to exhaust themselves,</b>

15:52.030 --> 15:53.620
<b>and launch a counterattack!</b>

15:54.010 --> 15:55.430
<b>This is a defensive battle!</b>

15:55.430 --> 15:57.630
<b>Keep your positions in good order!</b>

15:57.630 --> 15:58.680
<b>Yes, ma'am!</b>

16:12.260 --> 16:16.580
<b>All units are in position 
and ready to intercept.</b>

16:16.920 --> 16:18.130
<b>Good.</b>

16:18.130 --> 16:20.100
<b>By the way, Lieutenant Tospan.</b>

16:20.100 --> 16:21.820
<b>Where's Captain Thon?</b>

16:21.820 --> 16:23.320
<b>Why is he not answering?</b>

16:23.660 --> 16:25.840
<b>Well, he's...</b>

16:25.840 --> 16:28.250
<b><i>He's leading a recon team.</i></b>

16:29.380 --> 16:31.910
<b>H-He wants to survey the terrain!</b>

16:31.910 --> 16:34.420
<b>He says an officer 
should see it for himself.</b>

16:34.670 --> 16:37.430
<b>Then do it before 
the fucking enemy gets here!</b>

16:37.430 --> 16:40.850
<b>Keep your men in shouting distance!</b>

16:40.850 --> 16:42.120
<b><i>But ma'am...</i></b>

16:42.120 --> 16:43.090
<b>Shut up!</b>

16:43.090 --> 16:45.010
<b>Turn over command to Lieutenant Grantz!</b>

16:45.010 --> 16:46.760
<b>Wait!</b>

16:46.760 --> 16:49.250
<b>An officer has the right to 
make his own decisions...</b>

16:49.250 --> 16:50.940
<b><i>I told you to shut up!</i></b>

16:50.940 --> 16:53.790
<b>I'm too busy to deal with your bullshit!</b>

16:53.790 --> 16:56.570
<b>From now on, Captain Thon 
is to be treated as MIA!</b>

16:56.570 --> 16:58.820
<b><i>But that's not fair...</i></b>

17:03.370 --> 17:06.090
<b>Useless goddamn morons...</b>

17:06.090 --> 17:09.340
<b>And the snow fell earlier 
than I expected...</b>

17:09.960 --> 17:13.150
<b>How do we get out of this?</b>

17:19.350 --> 17:23.380
<b><i>How come none of the units 
are reporting enemy contact?</i></b>

17:24.330 --> 17:26.940
<b><i>The enemy's still waiting to attack?</i></b>

17:26.940 --> 17:29.490
<b><i>Are they continuing their encirclement?</i></b>

17:29.490 --> 17:32.200
<b><i>Should I try to attack and 
see how they respond?</i></b>

17:33.120 --> 17:36.300
<b><i>Major Weiss, can you 
do artillery spotting?</i></b>

17:37.280 --> 17:40.900
<b>In this darkness, I can't 
promise it'll be accurate.</b>

17:40.900 --> 17:42.430
<b>I thought so.</b>

17:42.430 --> 17:44.260
<b>Maybe I should wait to see 
what the enemy does...</b>

17:44.260 --> 17:45.170
<b><i>Lieutenant Colonel!</i></b>

17:45.170 --> 17:46.650
<b>Let us try!</b>

17:46.650 --> 17:49.280
<b>We've trained hard for 
night artillery combat.</b>

17:49.280 --> 17:50.430
<b>Okay.</b>

17:50.850 --> 17:54.350
<b>Open fire as soon as 
Major Weiss gives the order.</b>

17:54.350 --> 17:57.420
<b>But don't use too many shells.</b>

17:57.420 --> 17:58.860
<b>Conserve your ammo.</b>

17:58.860 --> 17:59.550
<b><i>Understood!</i></b>

18:00.490 --> 18:02.050
<b>Sharing coordinates!</b>

18:02.050 --> 18:03.510
<b><i>A8C6!</i></b>

18:03.510 --> 18:05.670
<b><i>I repeat! A8C6!</i></b>

18:05.680 --> 18:07.310
<b>Load the guns!</b>

18:07.680 --> 18:08.900
<b>Fire!</b>

18:18.650 --> 18:23.160
<b>Imperial Army 203rd Aerial Mage Battalion Vice-Commander and Salamander Combat Team Vice Commander
Major Matheus Johann Weiss</b>

18:19.190 --> 18:20.270
<b><i>Any effect?</i></b>

18:21.200 --> 18:23.160
<b>The effect is unknown.</b>

18:23.160 --> 18:25.440
<b>The darkness is worse than expected.</b>

18:27.330 --> 18:29.430
<b>All units, stay sharp.</b>

18:29.430 --> 18:32.070
<b>Stay in position until further orders!</b>

18:32.070 --> 18:34.260
<b>Don't let the enemy lure you out!
It's a waiting game now!</b>

18:56.280 --> 18:58.840
<b>Lieutenant Colonel, this is strange.</b>

18:58.840 --> 18:59.980
<b>What is?</b>

19:00.420 --> 19:02.230
<b>It's strangely silent.</b>

19:02.530 --> 19:05.240
<b>What is the enemy trying to do?</b>

19:05.670 --> 19:07.220
<b>I don't know.</b>

19:07.220 --> 19:09.240
<b>We can't see anything from here.</b>

19:09.740 --> 19:12.450
<b><i>Why? Why aren't they attacking?</i></b>

19:12.450 --> 19:15.280
<b><i>Is this whole thing just a 
decoy to keep us pinned down?</i></b>

19:15.750 --> 19:16.970
<b><i>This is 02!</i></b>

19:16.970 --> 19:18.500
<b><i>The situation has become clearer!</i></b>

19:18.500 --> 19:20.880
<b>These aren't brigades.</b>

19:20.880 --> 19:22.990
<b>They're what used to be brigades.</b>

19:22.990 --> 19:24.000
<b><i>What?</i></b>

19:24.410 --> 19:28.520
<b>The enemy was moving in tight groups, 
within voice range.</b>

19:28.860 --> 19:32.510
<b>So it appears our artillery 
wiped them out!</b>

19:34.050 --> 19:38.000
<b>So the Federation's brigades didn't 
get enough training time, either?</b>

19:38.970 --> 19:42.240
<b>Everybody, looks like 
we've been waiting for nothing.</b>

19:42.240 --> 19:45.150
<b>Show 'em what we've got, everybody!</b>

19:48.110 --> 19:51.420
<b>Number one through number five,
 sustained fire!</b>

19:51.420 --> 19:53.620
<b>Let's work enough to pay for that ammo!</b>

19:53.620 --> 19:56.040
<b>Panzer vor!</b>

20:01.060 --> 20:03.330
<b>Let's go! Time for the 
infantry to go to work!</b>

20:09.930 --> 20:12.410
<b>The infantry have begun their assault.</b>

20:12.410 --> 20:14.980
<b>We will proceed to wipe out the enemy.</b>

20:14.980 --> 20:18.820
<b>Got it. I want you to take command 
of Lt. Wüstemann's unit too.</b>

20:18.820 --> 20:21.030
<b>I want to fix their lack of training.</b>

20:21.030 --> 20:22.710
<b><i>Yes, ma'am. Immediately!</i></b>

20:24.290 --> 20:26.730
<b>That wraps that up.</b>

20:27.420 --> 20:31.750
<b>Looks like I might have 
to rethink things.</b>

20:34.590 --> 20:37.000
<b>Good work, everyone!</b>

20:42.250 --> 20:47.010
<b>The Lieutenant Colonel is 
giving us an innocent smile.</b>

20:50.470 --> 20:53.450
<b>First, very good work today, 
Captain Meybert!</b>

20:53.450 --> 20:56.070
<b>I want to show my respect 
for your talents!</b>

20:57.810 --> 21:01.420
<b>I was wrong about you!</b>

21:01.420 --> 21:04.820
<b>I hope you'll accept my apologies!</b>

21:04.820 --> 21:07.040
<b>Of course, ma'am!</b>

21:07.470 --> 21:09.440
<b>And you too, Captain Ahrens!</b>

21:09.440 --> 21:12.710
<b>Your last charge can only 
be described as impeccable!</b>

21:12.710 --> 21:14.310
<b>Thank you!</b>

21:14.310 --> 21:16.070
<b>And Lieutenant Wüstemann...</b>

21:16.070 --> 21:18.030
<b>I hope you'll grow into your role!</b>

21:18.030 --> 21:18.840
<b>Ma'am!</b>

21:19.810 --> 21:21.480
<b>As for Lieutenant Tospan,</b>

21:21.480 --> 21:24.080
<b>I'm not completely satisfied...</b>

21:24.340 --> 21:25.570
<b>But that's okay!</b>

21:25.570 --> 21:27.310
<b>Make up for it next time!</b>

21:27.310 --> 21:29.800
<b>I-I'll do my best!</b>

21:43.170 --> 21:47.700
<b><i>Did you think I'd change my opinion 
of you all after that performance?</i></b>

21:48.870 --> 21:53.330
<b><i>For better or for worse, 
I'm a high-ranking military officer.</i></b>

21:54.220 --> 21:56.820
<b><i>If we win the war,</i></b>

21:56.820 --> 21:59.020
<b><i>I'll get all the credit I want.</i></b>

22:04.990 --> 22:07.210
<b><i>But if we can't win...</i></b>

22:07.520 --> 22:10.710
<b><i>I'll be the one to take the blame.</i></b>

22:12.720 --> 22:17.260
<b><i>Given that I don't know how much leeway
 I'll get for just following orders,</i></b>

22:17.260 --> 22:21.730
<b><i>that means that other people's testimony 
will be what determines my fate.</i></b>

22:22.540 --> 22:28.270
<b><i>So from now on, I must focus on 
maintaining a good reputation and image.</i></b>

22:30.000 --> 22:33.540
<b>Wait, where is that oaf,
 Captain Thon?</b>

22:33.540 --> 22:37.530
<b>You're right. I haven't 
seen a report from him.</b>

22:37.530 --> 22:40.720
<b>He was captured, or he's dead.</b>

22:41.150 --> 22:42.370
<b>Well...</b>

22:42.370 --> 22:45.300
<b>If he deserted, he gets a firing squad.</b>

22:48.180 --> 22:51.220
<b>All right, everyone, let's have a toast!</b>

22:51.220 --> 22:52.590
<b>To our fatherland!</b>

22:53.070 --> 22:55.150
<b>To the victory of the Empire—</b>

22:56.920 --> 22:58.090
<b>No...</b>

22:58.370 --> 23:02.090
<b>To an early end to our war!</b>

23:02.090 --> 23:04.600
<b>Cheers!</b>

23:17.590 --> 23:20.580
<b>This... You're kidding, right?</b>

23:20.580 --> 23:22.820
<b>I'm afraid it's true.</b>

23:22.820 --> 23:25.330
<b>It's everywhere in the capital, I'm told.</b>

23:25.780 --> 23:28.590
<b>In the language of flowers, 
a gladiolus means victory.</b>

23:28.590 --> 23:31.720
<b>And olives, supposedly, 
are a symbol of peace.</b>

23:32.390 --> 23:34.340
<b>Propaganda is...</b>

23:34.350 --> 23:40.050
<b>"Peace is the greatest good"</b>

23:35.070 --> 23:37.260
<b>really scary.</b>
